{
  "source": "/tmp/oriole-value-fuzz/fuzz/fuzz_targets/value_family.rs",
  "source_sha256": "8ff2555325b0908d11fb9779d5cc653c901bf0e5611188f58ae7b7fc7d31691c",
  "conclusion": "No source-level blocker found for the bounded callback-driven harness; build, seed replay and sustained sanitizer campaign are separate required validation.",
  "review": [
    "Fixed eight-slot Family remains at a stable address until every parser and encoding registration is released. Slot is reserved before child creation or parsing, so nested callbacks cannot overwrite its state.",
    "Callback-visible state uses raw pointers and copies scalar fields before callback-capable C API calls. Immutable fuzzer input spans outlive all retained children and do not borrow Family.",
    "Allocator helpers track successful live allocations and fail selected allocation without losing realloc ownership; free(null) is ignored; end-of-case LIVE and encoding registration counters detect leaks and duplicate releases.",
    "Child depth<=4, request<=64, slot<=8, per-document feed<=4096, resume<=8 and payload<=65536 bound work; controls[16+slot] stays within32 controlbytes.",
    "Retained children can be finalized after root free/reset, then handles are freed in either order. Slots remain live throughout; external handler is disabled during detached-child feeding to keep cleanup nonrecursive.",
    "New depth selector directs callback actions into value-child depth2; all seven added XMLdecl seeds enable XMLdecl handler and choose depth2.",
    "Reviewed four additional fixed declaration-grammar templates under control25&7 and sixteen handler-presence seeds. Only literal selection and seed bytes changed; slot/lifetime bounds remain unchanged. Includes absent Default with PE-provided quoted value and skipped grammar before/after suspended value."
  ],
